    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Neutral atoms barely interact in their qubit states. Briefly excite one into a high Rydberg state, and its strong long-range interaction can shift a neighbor out of resonance. That is Rydberg blockade.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Explain Rydberg blockade without hard-coding one experiment's numbers.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — NEUTRAL ATOMS",
            "segment": "Interaction Shifts a Resonance",
            "greeting": "Yá'át'ééh, Liam",
            "runningText": "following the two-atom energy levels…",
            "output": [
              "One Rydberg excitation shifts the double-excitation level.",
              "A narrow resonant drive can no longer excite the neighbor."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Each atom has a qubit manifold and a highly excited Rydberg level. A laser is tuned to drive the chosen ground-to-Rydberg transition.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "With neither atom excited, the single-excitation transitions are resonant. Either atom can be promoted by the drive.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Excite atom A. Two simultaneous Rydberg atoms interact strongly, so the energy of the doubly excited state shifts by an amount V of their separation and chosen Rydberg levels.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "morph"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The same laser is now detuned from B's transition into the double-excitation state. When the interaction shift is large compared with the drive bandwidth, B's Rydberg excitation is strongly suppressed.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Blockade is therefore spectral, not a mechanical wall. Atom A changes an energy gap; it does not physically swell until it touches atom B.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "The interaction may behave like resonant dipole-dipole coupling or an off-resonant van der Waals interaction, depending on levels, fields, and distance. The scaling is not one universal n-to-the-four over r-cubed law.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "A blockade-based gate uses that conditional resonance. The target's pulse follows a different evolution depending on whether the control atom occupies the Rydberg state.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Real performance also depends on laser errors, atomic motion, finite Rydberg lifetime, imperfect blockade, and state preparation. No single radius, shift, or gate time describes every neutral-atom platform.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. Why is the second excitation suppressed? Pause before the answer: the first Rydberg atom shifts the double-excitation energy, so the fixed laser becomes off resonance when that shift exceeds the relevant drive bandwidth.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: state the blockade condition in words.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Shift Versus Bandwidth",
            "greeting": "Over to you, Liam",
            "runningText": "waiting for the spectral explanation…",
            "output": [
              "First excitation shifts the |rr> level.",
              "Large shift relative to drive bandwidth suppresses the second excitation."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
